+The formal composition vector of a compound records, for each primitive label $c$, the sum of its positive scale coefficients. Two compounds have the same composition exactly when these vectors agree. The distinct **formal mass** $m(A)$ is the sum of all scale coefficients in $A$, a dimensionless bookkeeping quantity; it is not physical mass in kilograms, mole amount, energy, or volume. Same-composition compounds have equal formal mass. For each compound type $T$, retain its full tuple state domain $D_T$, including its tags and factorization data. For each ordered pair $T,T'$ of equal composition, the model supplies a whole-compound process model with configuration set $Z_{T,T'}$, equilibrium endpoint subsets $Z^-_{T,T'},Z^+_{T,T'}$, and maps $\xi^-:Z^-_{T,T'}\to D_T$, $\xi^+:Z^+_{T,T'}\to D_{T'}$. It also supplies control/contact and transfer-record sets $\mathcal K_{T,T'}$, $\mathcal R_{T,T'}$, a chosen outer boundary accounting for all auxiliaries and devices. Physical energy bookkeeping uses its declared fixed Galilean chart; a purely formal thermometer model instead retains its explicitly declared numerical energy/unit maps and does not assert a material realization. An admitted record is a model-selected tuple $P=(I,A,B,z,\kappa,r)$, where $I=[t_0,t_1]$ is a finite positive-duration interval, $A\in D_T$, $B\in D_{T'}$, $z:I\to Z_{T,T'}$, $\kappa\in\mathcal K_{T,T'}$, $r\in\mathcal R_{T,T'}$, $z(t_0)\in Z^-_{T,T'}$, $z(t_1)\in Z^+_{T,T'}$, $\xi^-(z(t_0))=A$, and $\xi^+(z(t_1))=B$. Supply its net heat and work maps and the full-record no-thermal-transfer predicate with the sign and consistency conventions of [[def-td-process-and-protocol]], and declare the required auxiliary/device endpoint conditions. No path regularity or first-law balance is inferred from this lift. For a single unchanged type this model agrees with the original single-system records and relation of [[def-td-adiabatic-accessibility]]. Write $A\prec B$ exactly when an admitted lifted record has these full tuple endpoints, satisfies those auxiliary/device conditions, and has no thermal transfer throughout the outer boundary. This definition also covers equal-composition splitting or transport between different type expressions. Permutation and reassociation transports carry the entire record data and preserve admission and transfers. No accessibility witness or tuple endpoint is inferred from the aggregate coordinate-addition map, which need not be injective. A later represented-state channel model that identifies several tuple factorizations must explicitly require its endpoint relation to descend through that representation, equivalently requiring the lifted tuple relation to be the pullback of its declared represented-state channel relation; no such quotient compatibility follows from addition alone.
 
 An equal-composition comparison is a comparison between states of types with the same formal composition vector. The later reaction-network definition may separately admit transitions between distinct composition types, but the mathematical supplier still requires equal formal mass at both endpoints. A physical application must state how its channel preserves the chosen formal mass and separately record its dimensioned conservation balances. The empty unit has one state and formal mass zero. No identity is imposed between a primitive type and a scaled tag, or between two different decompositions of a compound, beyond the explicitly declared reassociation, permutation, and bulk-composition maps.
